"""tpa-bus-kinds: LOOK ONLY. Which buses say what kind of bus they are? (owner 10 Nov 11:08: "as much info as we
can at this stage to determine getting the right pics to the right buses")

Downloads the national BODS bus file ONCE (the same file the bus engine fetches every minute, with the same key from
/etc/tpa/bus.env), then lists every piece of information the buses send and how many buses send it - especially
seats, wheelchair spaces, occupancy and anything naming a vehicle type. Changes nothing; never prints the key.

Run on the server:  sudo python3 tpa-bus-kinds
Test with a saved file:  python3 tpa-bus-kinds --file bulk.zip

Part 2 (owner 11:12: the live feed sends no seats at all): --timetables looks in each big company's own timetable
files (TransXChange), which may name the vehicle type for each journey (Operational/VehicleType). One dataset per
company, fetched through the BODS timetable API with the same key; still look only.
  sudo python3 tpa-bus-kinds --timetables          (or: --timetables FYOR,TFLO to choose companies)
  python3 tpa-bus-kinds --txc-file some.zip         (test)
Part 3: --fleet lists the fleet numbers each company sends (look only).
Part 5: --fleetlists checks TfL's and East Yorkshire's published fleet lists against the live buses.
Part 4: --calibrate [NOC,NOC] matches live buses to their timetabled journeys and counts which fleet numbers run which kind.
"""
